{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1310,
    "dDurationMs": 4811,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When it's cold out and you didn't dress for\nthe weather and you're far from shelter, you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6121,
    "dDurationMs": 5119,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have a crucial decision to make: should you\nrun (or ski) to try to warm up, or go slow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11240,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and avoid the cooling effects of wind?\nWhen it's cold out and you're not moving,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15850,
    "dDurationMs": 5169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the heat you lose goes to heating up the air\naround you, forming a slightly warmer protective"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21019,
    "dDurationMs": 4571,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "layer so you don't cool off as quickly. But\nif you're moving (or if it's windy), you’re"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25590,
    "dDurationMs": 5009,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "being exposed to some amount of fresh, new,\ncold air – more of it the faster you go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30599,
    "dDurationMs": 4191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You’re literally running away from the air\nyou warmed and so you cool off faster than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34790,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you stayed put.\nThough once you're going fast enough, the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37610,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "protective layer of air will be pretty much\nentirely gone and you'll basically lose heat"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41660,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the same rate regardless of how fast you're\nrunning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44180,
    "dDurationMs": 4730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, when humans run, we also generate a fair\namount of heat inside our bodies. In fact,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48910,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we produce a roughly constant amount of heat\nper kilometer traveled, so the faster you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53080,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "go, the more heat you generate any given minute.\nBecause the heat generated by running has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58120,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a steady increase, while your protective layer\nof warm air goes away quickly at low speeds,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63400,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it turns out that there's a kind of \"forbidden\nrange\" of speeds where it's not worth walking,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68240,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or even running slowly, since you’d lose\nless heat standing still."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72670,
    "dDurationMs": 3909,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what's the minimum speed where the heat\nyou generate running finally balances out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76579,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the additional heat you lose due to air movement?\nWell, using some estimations for the surface"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81049,
    "dDurationMs": 5070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "area and energy generation of an adult human\nrunning naked and the effects of wind on heat"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86119,
    "dDurationMs": 5020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "loss, I found that when it's freezing outside\n, you need to be able to run roughly a 5 minute"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91139,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mile to be better off moving than staying\nput. And faster, if it’s colder out. And"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95549,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this wouldn’t even mean you're not losing\nheat – it's just the point at which you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98549,
    "dDurationMs": 3041,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lose less heat running than you do standing\nstill."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101590,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now if that sounds like a challenge, don't\nworry. All you need to do is put on some clothing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106470,
    "dDurationMs": 4069,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– like, enough that you're only losing half\nas much heat as a naked person – and a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110539,
    "dDurationMs": 3801,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "15 minute mile (basically a brisk walk), will\ndo just fine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114340,
    "dDurationMs": 6389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, either stay put, or wear appropriate winter\nclothing, or run naked very very fast through"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120729,
    "dDurationMs": 680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the snow."
    } ]
  } ]
}
